{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3133127,"ns":0,"title":"Fáry–Milnor theorem","extract":"In the mathematical theory of knots, the Fáry–Milnor theorem, named after István Fáry and John Milnor, states that three-dimensional smooth curves with small total curvature must be unknotted. The theorem was proved independently by Fáry in 1949 and Milnor in 1950.","description":"Three-dimensional smooth curves with small total curvature must be unknotted","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}